<!-- Lucide "stamp" - the project's only icon set. See docs/ui-guidelines.md.
     Stroke is white; every use tints it via Icon(tint = ...).

     ⚠ **Replaces "sparkles" on the Automatic labels row, 2026-09-03, and the reason is not
     taste.** Sparkles has become the universal mark for "an AI did this". Sika's automatic
     labels are the opposite of that: nothing is inferred, guessed or generated. You ticked
     "always label this way" on one transaction, and Sika repeats exactly that instruction.

     The icon mattered more than it looks because of Sacred Rule 12 - the LLM never sees the
     ledger. An icon implying a model had a hand in labelling his money is a claim the app
     goes to some trouble not to make.

     A stamp is the same mark applied again, which is precisely the feature. The runners-up
     and why they lost, so nobody re-litigates this: "repeat" and "rotate-cw" both read as
     sync or refresh, which implies a network in an app that has no INTERNET permission at
     all; "check-check" is the cleanest of the six at 19dp but says "done", not "done for
     you"; "bookmark-check" says saved, not repeated. -->
